# Pre-delivery checklist

Run this before showing any UI to Angel. If any line fails, fix it first.

## Non-negotiables
- [ ] Zero divider lines (`border-bottom`, `<hr>`, `divide-y`, dotted/dashed separators). Separation is spacing / tonal surface / active-highlight only.
- [ ] Zero glow (no colored box-shadow halos, no neon edges, no "pop" glow).
- [ ] Every shadow present is functional (floating media, scroll-state, or carousel arrow affordance). No default-decoration shadows.
- [ ] No media is letterboxed/padded onto a solid background. All art is `object-fit: cover`, cropped, rounded.
- [ ] Depth reads through a tonal surface ramp (surface-0 → surface-3), not effects.
- [ ] Characterful sans in use (Satoshi/General Sans/Cabinet), not Inter/system-ui default.
- [ ] Base is a tonal hue, not pure `#000`/`#fff`.

## System
- [ ] Radius is tiered (outer rounder than nested; pills on chips/actions; soft-rect on primary CTA).
- [ ] Color contract set: theme mode matches task (media=dark, info=light), one accent, mode = MONOCHROME or CODED.
- [ ] Gradient/saturation only on media/hero, never chrome.
- [ ] Spacing preset chosen per surface (compact for tools, airy for hero/empty), from a 4px ramp.
- [ ] Type hierarchy uses weight + muted color (not just size); one hero; tiny uppercase labels for metadata.
- [ ] Motion uses transform/opacity only; fast+eased default; spring only on signature moments; reduced-motion respected.

## Media (if applicable)
- [ ] Card aspect ratio matches content type (poster 2:3 vs resume 16:9 vs square 1:1).
- [ ] Positional info follows convention (duration bottom-right, rank top-left, metadata dot-line under card).
- [ ] Sections that differ in value look different (no clone rows).
- [ ] Nav solid; search/overlay glassy. Blur picked by element role.

## Voice
- [ ] Empty states are casual-human and point at the next action.
- [ ] Functional/settings screens are precise and plain (no jokes).

## The gut check
- [ ] For every non-obvious visual element, you can answer: "what does this signal?" If the answer is "nothing," remove it.
